nora (docs): Quick PR incoming to update streaming/pagination snippets across Py/TS/Go: show resume tokens, discourage naive restarts, and add a short retry-policy blob. Need a quick review.

ben (sdk): Good. Prefer showing low-level patterns (for clarity) and a note pointing to the higher-level `resume()` helper.

aliya (devex): Draft Python async snippet (lint-friendly comment included):
```python
# from rwd import Client
# client = Client()  # reuse per process
async def stream_resumable(prompt):
    token = load_token()  # may be None
    async for ev in client.responses.stream(model='rwd/sm-1', input=prompt, resume_token=token):
        if ev.type == 'delta':
            print(ev.text, end='')
        elif ev.type == 'resume_token':
            save_token(ev.token)
```
Note: don't persist sensitive user content in resume storage.

sam (eng): Add a billing caveat: full restarts can duplicate output and double-bill. Recommend idempotency keys or server offsets for Dedicated customers.

ben (sdk): TS pattern (wrap in async function to avoid top-level await issues):
```ts
async function run() {
  const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'rwd/sm-1', input, cursor: await readCursor() });
  for await (const e of stream) {
    if (e.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(e.text);
    if (e.type === 'cursor') { await writeCursor(e.cursor); }
  }
}
```
Include a short reconnect/backoff note rather than code to avoid encouraging naive loops.

aliya (devex): Go iterator example (pseudo-types):
```go
it := client.StreamResponses(ctx, &Request{Model: "rwd/sm-1", Input: input, Cursor: saved})
for it.Next() {
  ev := it.Event()
  switch ev.Type {
  case "delta": fmt.Print(ev.Text)
  case "cursor": persistCursor(ev.Cursor)
  }
}
if err := it.Err(); err != nil { log.Printf("stream error: %v", err) }
```

ben (sdk): Add docs-only pseudo-config for recommended retry policy: `max_retries: 3, initial_backoff_ms: 200, backoff_factor: 2, resume_on_cursor: true, avoid_full_restart_unless_idempotent: true`.

